WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.355
The industrial DMZ is commonly described as Level 3.5.

00:00:04.355 --> 00:00:07.490
It is a security extension to the traditional Purdue discussion,

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.890
not an original numbered level.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:13.100
Its purpose is to create a controlled buffer between enterprise IT and site operations so

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.180
ordinary enterprise systems do not communicate directly with control networks.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.370
Services in the industrial DMZ mediate necessary exchange.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.235
A jump host can provide a managed path for administration.

00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:27.245
A remote-access broker can enforce identity, approval, and session controls.

00:00:27.245 --> 00:00:31.120
Patch and antivirus repositories can stage content before it enters OT.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.910
Data replication services can move historian information outward without allowing

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.510
enterprise clients to query control systems directly.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.140
Monitoring, logging, authentication proxies, file-transfer services,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.620
and update gateways may also belong in this zone.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.760
The exact design depends on operations, but each service should have a narrow purpose.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.880
Connections should specify approved sources, destinations, protocols, direction,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.640
and owner. Broad routing through the DMZ defeats the reason for having it.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.530
The DMZ is not automatically trusted.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:01.680
It faces connections from two environments and may contain high-value access services.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.080
Harden systems, separate administrative access, monitor traffic, patch deliberately,

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.935
retain logs, and avoid using the zone as a general-purpose server network.

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:13.920
Remote sessions should terminate or be proxied there rather than passing transparently

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:14.520
into OT.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.120
A strong industrial DMZ reduces direct enterprise-to-control connectivity and creates

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.600
inspection points for data and control flows.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.905
It cannot repair weak segmentation below Level 3 or poor identity governance above it.

00:01:25.905 --> 00:01:29.632
Think of it as one architectural layer in a broader defense that includes controlled

00:01:29.632 --> 00:01:33.200
pathways, least privilege, asset knowledge, and operational oversight.
